      "explanation": "<img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1li1gqkm9/49f62ce3-5e8c-4e0c-a038-a8e8e92393ef/c0757510-fa0f-11ed-a67c-fd44bcb96a53/file-1li1gqkma.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1li1gqkm9/49f62ce3-5e8c-4e0c-a038-a8e8e92393ef/c0757510-fa0f-11ed-a67c-fd44bcb96a53/file-1li1gqkma.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Advanced 2017 Paper 1 Offline Chemistry - Aldehydes, Ketones and Carboxylic Acids Question 74 English Explanation 1\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1li1gqkm9/49f62ce3-5e8c-4e0c-a038-a8e8e92393ef/c0757510-fa0f-11ed-a67c-fd44bcb96a53/file-1li1gqkma.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1li1gqkm9/49f62ce3-5e8c-4e0c-a038-a8e8e92393ef/c0757510-fa0f-11ed-a67c-fd44bcb96a53/file-1li1gqkma.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1li1gqkm9/49f62ce3-5e8c-4e0c-a038-a8e8e92393ef/c0757510-fa0f-11ed-a67c-fd44bcb96a53/file-1li1gqkma.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1li1gqkm9/49f62ce3-5e8c-4e0c-a038-a8e8e92393ef/c0757510-fa0f-11ed-a67c-fd44bcb96a53/file-1li1gqkma.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1li1gqkm9/49f62ce3-5e8c-4e0c-a038-a8e8e92393ef/c0757510-fa0f-11ed-a67c-fd44bcb96a53/file-1li1gqkma.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1li1gqkm9/49f62ce3-5e8c-4e0c-a038-a8e8e92393ef/c0757510-fa0f-11ed-a67c-fd44bcb96a53/file-1li1gqkma.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\">\n<br>Reaction of benzaldehyde with acetic\nanhydride in presence of potassium acetate\nresults in formation of cinnamic acid. Cinnamic\nacid contains cis and trans forms; hence, two\ntypes of acids are generated. This is called\nPerkin reaction.\n<br><br>Mechanism of Perkin reaction is as follows :\n<br